.TH MU2EDAQ-DATAFORMAT-FORMATS.YAML 5 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-dataformat-formats.yaml \- packet layout definitions in formats/*.yaml
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I formats/<packet>.yaml
.br
.I formats/packet_type_index.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each file describes one Mu2e ROC packet layout, transcribed by hand from
Mu2e-doc-4914 (the copy shipped as
.IR doc/mu2e\-dataformat.pdf ,
V53, 21 Feb 2026).
Both GUIs load every
.I *.yaml
in
.B formats_dir
with
.BR yaml.safe_load ,
skip
.IR packet_type_index.yaml ,
and key each format by its
.BR name .
A file that fails to parse is reported on stdout and skipped.
There is no schema validation and no comparison with the C++ overlays in
artdaq-core-mu2e, which encode the same layouts independently.
.SS Top-level keys
.TP
.B name
Display name and lookup key; must be unique.
The viewer's auto-detect table expects the names
.BR "DCS Request Packet" ,
.BR "Heartbeat Packet" ,
.BR "Data Request Packet" ,
.BR "Prefetch Request Packet" ,
.BR "DCS Reply Packet" ,
.BR "Data Header Packet" ,
.BR "Data Payload Packet" ,
.B "DCS Request Additional Block Write Payload Packet"
and
.BR "DCS Reply Additional Block Read Payload Packet" .
.TP
.B packet_type
4-bit type code (informational; the GUIs do not read it).
.TP
.B size_bytes
Buffer size used by the sender.
Fields beyond it are not written.
.TP
.B fields
List of field definitions (below).
.TP
.BR packet_1 ", " packet_2
Sub-sections, each with
.B description
and
.BR fields ,
decoded one after the other from the same offset (tracker).
.TP
.B hit_format
Sub-section with
.BR fields ;
used by the sender only.
.TP
.BR description ", " notes ", " serial_header ", " dma_channel ", " subsystem_id ", " subsystem_name ", ..."
Documentation only.
Other structures
.RB ( hit_header ,
.BR waveform_samples ,
.BR formats ,
\&...) are not interpreted; the calorimeter hit, calorimeter hit debugging
and CRV hit formats therefore show an empty table in the viewer.
.SS Field keys
.TP
.B name
Shown in the table.
A name containing
.B reserved
(any case) is greyed.
.TP
.B word
16-bit word index from the decode offset (byte offset = 2 \(mu word).
.TP
.B bits
.B \(dqH:L\(dq
or
.BR \(dqN\(dq ,
bit positions within the word, 15 = most significant.
The width is computed from this; quote it so YAML keeps it a string.
.TP
.B size_bits
Width; used by the sender for formatting only.
Must equal H\-L+1 (true for all 229 shipped top-level fields).
.TP
.B fixed_value
Expected value; the viewer colours the row green or red, the sender
pre-fills and locks it.
.TP
.B values
Map from value (int or hex string) to label.
.TP
.B subfields
List of
.BR name ,
.BR bits ,
.BR description ,
.BR values ;
bit numbers are absolute word positions.
Displayed as text only, not decoded.
.TP
.BR description ", " notes
Free text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
name: Example Packet
packet_type: 0x5
size_bytes: 16
fields:
  \- name: Byte Count
    word: 0
    bits: "15:0"
    size_bits: 16
    description: Transfer byte count.
  \- name: Packet Type
    word: 1
    bits: "7:4"
    size_bits: 4
    fixed_value: 0x5
    description: Always 5.
.fi
.SH BUGS
The heartbeat, data-request and debug-header files disagree with the
specification and with artdaq-core-mu2e; see
.IR doc/INTERFACES.md
and DFV-001 in
.IR doc/ISSUES\-PENDING.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-sender.py (1),
.BR mu2e\-viewer.yaml (5)
